#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241017 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119856 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28acedc8-6185-5174-a20f-1523f6e81664" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238413} {:answer/id #uuid "911bf0a4-bca6-575a-8b8e-b3222ff2700c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239312} {:answer/id #uuid "aa49ecea-790f-512b-a264-3f8fef658cd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239546} {:answer/id #uuid "deff7940-817f-5ec1-8070-a43c35299f4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240003} {:answer/id #uuid "e11c88b3-593a-53f2-8807-09f826099a04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "deff7940-817f-5ec1-8070-a43c35299f4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240003} :answer-field/id #uuid "b832e88e-aa6a-556d-b56a-7bd0240d9f74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240651}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4e417e2f-54d8-52fa-a283-38ee2e22e96c" :question/math-academy-id "q-105232" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -7 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -7 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=8 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2}=-7 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+8.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+8\\,⇒\\,k=-8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241019 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119856 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "351d3eaa-8d71-5eaf-91f1-6a15d982842b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238515} {:answer/id #uuid "521c8347-9356-57c0-82a2-f6f058e2fdd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238763} {:answer/id #uuid "77e423df-6336-5ebd-a988-70ffd97ff91b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239089} {:answer/id #uuid "9e933237-ff23-52d2-a25d-7ee910ab795d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239441} {:answer/id #uuid "b70c1cd0-e286-53f1-ba39-4e8669a377a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "521c8347-9356-57c0-82a2-f6f058e2fdd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238763} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca08aa7d-69a4-53e7-9a42-33232fc442bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "847914f8-60db-55a2-9155-7cfe231e6bcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-105237" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=-6 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+12{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 12 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+9.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+9\\,⇒\\,k=-9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317208 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119809 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08ca81bd-a843-517f-a7ef-72a2701907bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315161} {:answer/id #uuid "31e52722-b368-5c85-8ea5-9c73d21f221f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315408} {:answer/id #uuid "3a3a18e5-9318-5ff6-9f5d-5297ea2e47b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315452} {:answer/id #uuid "43670fca-c17e-5839-b7bf-2ab9ba603b7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315509} {:answer/id #uuid "8a0a632c-b0f2-53fa-9828-61b94974deed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43670fca-c17e-5839-b7bf-2ab9ba603b7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315509} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed15606e-311e-585d-8930-70b904dd77b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317109}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "725d2e8b-44d5-5b25-872e-7c29b876b698" :question/math-academy-id "q-34212" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,7,-3⟩$, $c=⟨-8,10,-4⟩$, and  $u=⟨6,9,-4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s-8t=6 \\\\ 7s+10t=9 \\\\ -3s-4t=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 10 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 66 & -33 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 66 & -33 \\\\ 0 & -28 & 14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{66}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & -28 & 14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+28{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s-8t=6 \\\\ t=-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s-8t & =6 \\\\ s-8(-\\frac{1}{2}) & =6 \\\\ s+4 & =6 \\\\ s & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=2,\\,t=-\\frac{1}{2},$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=2b-\\frac{1}{2}c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342231 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119856 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4823cb09-c970-5693-9e2b-8bd1376d913d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339771} {:answer/id #uuid "80e4ce86-252f-55b0-9c33-fb68673d04ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340284} {:answer/id #uuid "acf2eadb-7cd8-54d4-a9e9-27a5f5fb57dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340703} {:answer/id #uuid "d1c084ff-7550-5511-af3c-c648fa93d138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340987} {:answer/id #uuid "f0a99f2f-8df2-5e11-8059-1ebda3f846e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1c084ff-7550-5511-af3c-c648fa93d138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340987} :answer-field/id #uuid "d24716d5-0fd3-56ef-817c-00602c395b53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341751}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1691e3c5-722a-5803-9898-54e9fb9a633f" :question/math-academy-id "q-74559" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+9{x}_{2}=-8 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 9 & -8 \\\\ -2 & 10 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 10 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 6 & k+6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-6{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-18\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-18.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-18\\,⇒\\,k=18.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342240 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119809 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18285e78-b775-52d3-9ce4-8875b58cd9dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339343} {:answer/id #uuid "1be7024d-e144-5979-8991-a6fe697cbc56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339367} {:answer/id #uuid "39886f7e-3d38-5ba7-ae30-319ca5a0cc0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339646} {:answer/id #uuid "7c3953fd-8be9-5eec-b885-1d99ddc7adf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340246} {:answer/id #uuid "bb9dd147-f938-5d4d-8bda-da9705de4409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1be7024d-e144-5979-8991-a6fe697cbc56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339367} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8ed9efb-9d03-53c8-9fad-57fa155b57a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341732}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "55c44296-8bfb-53c1-b37c-07eab30d99a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-74598" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,2,3⟩$, $c=⟨3,-7,-9⟩$, and  $u=⟨2,-3,-6⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+3t=2 \\\\ 2s-7t=-3 \\\\ 3s-9t=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -7 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+3t=2 \\\\ -t=1 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-t=1\\,⟹\\,t=-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+3t & =2 \\\\ -s+3(-1) & =2 \\\\ -s & =5 \\\\ s & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-5,\\,t=-1,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-5b-c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-5)\\cdot (-1)=5.$"}]}
